<div class="page-section-wrapper position-relative page-section-frequently-asked-questions">
      <div class="page-section-anchor" id="frequently-asked-questions-1373016"></div>
  
    
  <div class="page-section page-section-frequently-asked-questions page-section-1373016 text-left"
      style="">
        <div class="container " style="">
                                


<div class="page-section-headline ">
                <h2 class="page-section-title text-center">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      
  </div>
        
        
                
              
                


        
    <ul class="expandable-list large list-unstyled ">
        
                      <div class=''>
        <li
          data-bs-toggle="collapse"
          data-bs-target="#expandable-list-answer-819-0"
          class="collapsed expanded-link "
          aria-expanded= "false"
          aria-controls="expandable-list-answer-819-0"
        >
          <span class='align-middle '>Is API access included with my Moz Pro plan?</span>
        </li>
        <li class="collapse expanded-content " id="expandable-list-answer-819-0">
         <div class="">
          <p>There is no paid access included in the Moz Pro subscription. However, we do offer free limited access to our API. <a href="/checkout/moz-api/plan/api_free">Sign up here</a>.</p>
        </div>
        </li>
      </div>
                      <div class=''>
        <li
          data-bs-toggle="collapse"
          data-bs-target="#expandable-list-answer-819-1"
          class="collapsed expanded-link "
          aria-expanded= "false"
          aria-controls="expandable-list-answer-819-1"
        >
          <span class='align-middle '>What is a row and how many do I need?</span>
        </li>
        <li class="collapse expanded-content " id="expandable-list-answer-819-1">
         <div class="">
          <p dir="ltr">Rows are how we measure the cost of API requests. The endpoint and parameters determine the number of rows used per call. Some endpoints, such as the Final Redirect endpoint, will always return a single-object result and consume one row of data. Other endpoints, such as Links and URL metrics, may return multiple results depending on the limit specified in the request parameters and/or the number of inputs provided. Usually, each object in the result counts as a single row of data, but some endpoints can consume more than one row per object. <a href="https://moz.com/help/links-api/making-calls/weighted-endpoints">Learn more about these weighted endpoints</a>.</p><p dir="ltr"><strong>To help estimate your row usage, here are a few sample scenarios:</strong></p><p dir="ltr">•<strong> Starter Medium plan</strong> (3000 rows/month): track URL metrics for 25 domains daily</p><p dir="ltr">• <strong>Growth Medium plan</strong> (120,000 rows/month): pull up to 100,000 links pointing at any target, track URL metrics for over 500 domains daily, and still have enough capacity to audit site migrations with Moz API’s Final Redirect endpoint or track your link acquisition campaigns with Link Status</p><p dir="ltr">• <strong>Advanced plan</strong> (4 million rows/month): perform backlink analysis and domain research at scale – with almost 130,000 rows per day, you could generate a Link Intersect Venn diagram of up to 500 links for six different domains, plus URL metrics with full daily and monthly histories for every metric for over 4,000 domains daily, with rows to spare.<br /> </p><p> </p>
        </div>
        </li>
      </div>
                      <div class=''>
        <li
          data-bs-toggle="collapse"
          data-bs-target="#expandable-list-answer-819-2"
          class="collapsed expanded-link "
          aria-expanded= "false"
          aria-controls="expandable-list-answer-819-2"
        >
          <span class='align-middle '>Can I upgrade to a paid plan from the Free plan?</span>
        </li>
        <li class="collapse expanded-content " id="expandable-list-answer-819-2">
         <div class="">
          Yes, you can upgrade your plan on the subscription page of the Moz API dashboard at any time.
        </div>
        </li>
      </div>
                      <div class=''>
        <li
          data-bs-toggle="collapse"
          data-bs-target="#expandable-list-answer-819-3"
          class="collapsed expanded-link "
          aria-expanded= "false"
          aria-controls="expandable-list-answer-819-3"
        >
          <span class='align-middle '>Can I connect Moz data to AI tools?</span>
        </li>
        <li class="collapse expanded-content " id="expandable-list-answer-819-3">
         <div class="">
          <p>Yes. The Moz MCP Server connects supported AI clients and coding agents to Moz data, helping you build faster. Instead of writing custom code, you can chat with your AI client while it calls the right Moz tools and retrieves data on your behalf.</p><p>MCP access is currently in beta for account owners with an eligible Moz Data API subscription.</p>
        </div>
        </li>
      </div>
                      <div class=''>
        <li
          data-bs-toggle="collapse"
          data-bs-target="#expandable-list-answer-819-4"
          class="collapsed expanded-link "
